eading and the rest have none: to change one at a breakpoint, wrap it in a Row or Column and put the breakpoint prop there (s={{ hide: true }}). Width props take a number, a spacing token or a CSS unit, never \"auto\": to undo a width at a breakpoint write s={{ fillWidth: true }} or s={{ width: \"100%\" }}. Text and Heading take padding but no radius, border or flex; put those on the wrapper.","size.rem":"A number on width, height, minWidth or minHeight is rem, not px: width={32} is 512 px. For a pixel size write the spacing token string, width=\"32\" (32 px), or the rem value, width={2}. Token strings stop at the spacing scale (\"160\" is the largest), so height=\"320\" is a type error: write height={20}. An icon or avatar box is usually \"24\" to \"48\".","spacing.tokens":"gap, padding and margin take spacing tokens (\"0\", \"1\", \"2\", \"4\", \"8\", \"12\", \"16\", \"20\", \"24\", \"32\", \"40\", \"48\", \"56\", \"64\", \"72\", \"80\", \"104\", \"128\", \"160\", or xs–xl). \"6\" and \"10\" are not tokens and are type errors.","layout.noSpanOrType":"Row, Column and Grid have no span and no type prop. A clickable row is a Button (or a native <button>), and a Grid child spanning columns uses style={{ gridColumn: \"span 2\" }}.","Checkbox.checked":"Checkbox, Switch and RadioButton take checked (or defaultChecked) and onToggle(checked: boolean). isChecked and isIndeterminate were 1.x; the 2.x props are checked and indeterminate."},"quality":{"pageHeader":"Title and one primary Button in a Row that stacks at s; per-record actions belong in the Table's actions, not the header","cellText":"A component cell (name with email, a status Tag) carries its text as children — Table searches and sorts by the text inside each cell","status":"Tag with a scheme and a text label, never colour alone","emptyState":"Offer the way back (clear the filter), not only 'No results'","rowActions":"Icon actions with tooltips; destructive ones take variant=\"danger\""},"mixins":{"CommonProps":{